<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="HEB" style="id">HEBREWS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="HEB 1"/>
  <para style="s1">God’s Final Word through His Son</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 1:1"/>
    In the past, God spoke to our fathers through the prophets in many portions and in a variety of ways,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 1:2"/>
    but in these last days He has spoken to us through His Son, whom He appointed as the heir of all things and through whom He also brought the entire created order into existence.
    <verse eid="HEB 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 1:3"/>
    He is the radiant outshining of God’s glory and the exact imprint of His very being, and He sustains all things by His powerful word. After accomplishing the cleansing of sins, He took His seat at the right hand of the supreme Majesty in heaven,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 1:4"/>
    having become far superior to the angels, just as the name He has received is far more excellent than theirs.
    <verse eid="HEB 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Supremacy of the Son over the Angels</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 1:5"/>
    For to which of the angels did God ever say,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are My Son;</para>
  <para style="p">today I have brought You forth?”*</para>
  <para style="p">And again,</para>
  <para style="p">“I will be a Father to Him,</para>
  <para style="p">and He will be a Son to Me?”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 1:6"/>
    And again, when God brings His firstborn into the world, He declares,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Let all the angels of God worship Him.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 1:7"/>
    With reference to the angels, He says,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“He makes His angels swift as winds,</para>
  <para style="p">and His servants like a flame of fire.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 1:8"/>
    But with reference to the Son, He says,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Your throne, O God, stands forever and ever,</para>
  <para style="p">and the sceptre of righteousness is the sceptre of Your kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 1:9"/>
    You have loved what is right and hated lawlessness;
    <verse eid="HEB 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">therefore God, Your God, has anointed You</para>
  <para style="p">with the oil of gladness above Your companions.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 1:10"/>
    And He also says,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You, Lord, laid the foundation of the earth at the beginning,</para>
  <para style="p">and the heavens are the work of Your hands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 1:11"/>
    They will perish, but You remain;
    <verse eid="HEB 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">they will all wear out like a garment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 1:12"/>
    Like a robe You will roll them up,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and like clothing they will be changed.</para>
  <para style="p">But You remain the same,</para>
  <para style="p">and Your years will never come to an end.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 1:13"/>
    And to which of the angels has He ever said,
    <verse eid="HEB 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Sit at My right hand</para>
  <para style="p">until I place Your enemies as a footstool for Your feet?”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 1:14"/>
    Are not all the angels ministering spirits, sent out by God to serve on behalf of those who are destined to inherit salvation?
    <verse eid="HEB 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Ps. 2:7</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from 2 Sam. 7:14; 1 Chr. 17:13; cf. Ps. 89:26-27</para>
  <para style="p">6 Quoted from the Septuagint of Deut. 32:43; cf. Ps. 97:7</para>
  <para style="p">7 Quoted from Ps. 104:4</para>
  <para style="p">8-9 Quoted from Ps. 45:6-7</para>
  <para style="p">10-12 Quoted from Ps. 102:25-27</para>
  <para style="p">13 Quoted from Ps. 110:1</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="HEB 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Neglecting Salvation</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 2:1"/>
    For this reason, we must pay much closer attention to what we have heard, so that we do not slowly drift away from it.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 2:2"/>
    For if the message delivered through angels proved firm and binding, and every violation and act of disobedience received a deserved judgment,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 2:3"/>
    how will we escape if we treat with indifference a salvation of such magnitude? This salvation was first proclaimed by the Lord Himself and was later confirmed to us by those who heard Him directly.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 2:4"/>
    God Himself also testified alongside them, confirming the message by signs, wonders, various mighty works, and by sovereignly distributing the gifts  of the Holy Spirit according to His own will.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Son Made Lower than Angels</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 2:5"/>
    For God has not given authority over the world to come—the world we are discussing—to angelic beings.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 2:6"/>
    Instead, Scripture records someone declaring,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“What is man that You hold him in Your mind,</para>
  <para style="p">or the son of man that You attend to him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 2:7"/>
    You made him temporarily below the angels in rank;
    <verse eid="HEB 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">You placed upon him a crown representing glory and honour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 2:8"/>
    You put all things under his feet.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">When God put everything under his control, He excluded nothing from this authority. Yet in our current situation, we do not yet see everything under his control.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 2:9"/>
    However, we do see Jesus, who was made below angels for a brief period, now wearing the crown of glory and honour because He suffered death. Through God’s gracious provision, He tasted death as the representative for every person.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Bringing Many Sons to Glory</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 2:10"/>
    For it was completely appropriate that God—the One for whose sake everything exists and through whose agency everything came into being—should lead many sons into glory by bringing the Pioneer of their salvation to completion through sufferings.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 2:11"/>
    For the One who makes people holy and those being made holy all originate from one source. This is why He feels no shame in addressing them as brothers and sisters,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 2:12"/>
    stating,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“I will make Your name known to My brothers and sisters;</para>
  <para style="p">within the gathered assembly I will sing praise to You.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 2:13"/>
    And in another passage,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“I will rest My confidence in Him.”*</para>
  <para style="p">And again,</para>
  <para style="p">“Here I stand with the children God has entrusted to Me.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 2:14"/>
    Since, therefore, the children participate fully in flesh and blood, He similarly partook of that same nature, so that through His death He might destroy the one holding death’s power, namely, the devil,
    <verse eid="HEB 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 2:15"/>
    and so that He might liberate all those who through their entire lives remained enslaved because of their fear of death.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 2:16"/>
    For clearly He does not reach out to help angels, but reaches out to help Abraham’s descendants.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 2:17"/>
    For this reason, it was necessary for Him to become similar to His brothers and sisters in all respects, so that He might prove to be a compassionate and trustworthy High Priest in matters pertaining to God, to accomplish propitiation for the people’s sins.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 2:18"/>
    For because He Himself experienced suffering under temptation, He has the capacity to assist those undergoing temptation.
    <verse eid="HEB 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">6-8 Quoted from Ps. 8:4-6</para>
  <para style="p">12 Quoted from Ps. 22:22</para>
  <para style="p">13 Quoted from Is. 8:17</para>
  <para style="p">13 Quoted from Is. 8:18</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="HEB 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Jesus, Greater Than Moses</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 3:1"/>
    Consequently, holy brothers and sisters who participate in a calling originating from heaven, direct your careful consideration towards Jesus, the Apostle and High Priest we openly acknowledge,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 3:2"/>
    who proved trustworthy to the One appointing Him, just as Moses also proved trustworthy throughout all of God’s household.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 3:3"/>
    For Jesus has been evaluated as deserving greater honour than Moses, in the same measure that a house’s builder deserves greater honour than the house he constructs.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 3:4"/>
    For every house receives construction from someone, but God is the One who constructed everything.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 3:5"/>
    Now Moses demonstrated trustworthiness throughout all of God's household in a servant’s capacity, providing testimony to things that would later be communicated.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 3:6"/>
    But Christ demonstrates trustworthiness in a Son’s capacity over God’s household—and we constitute His household, provided we retain our bold confidence and our hope’s boast.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against an Evil Heart of Unbelief</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 3:7"/>
    Therefore, exactly as the Holy Spirit communicates,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Today, should you perceive His voice,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 3:8"/>
    do not make your hearts rigid as during the rebellion,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">during that testing day in the wilderness,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 3:9"/>
    where your ancestors put Me to the test
    <verse eid="HEB 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and observed My works across forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 3:10"/>
    Therefore, I grew angry with that generation,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and I declared, ‘Their hearts perpetually wander,</para>
  <para style="p">and they have failed to comprehend My ways.’</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 3:11"/>
    Just as I swore in My anger,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">‘They will absolutely not enter My rest.’ ”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 3:12"/>
    Take care, brothers and sisters, lest there develop in any among you a wicked heart characterised by unbelief, resulting in falling away from the living God.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 3:13"/>
    Instead, provide mutual encouragement daily, while it continues to be designated “Today,” so that none among you becomes calloused through sin’s deception.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 3:14"/>
    For we have become Christ’s partners, assuming we maintain our initial confidence securely to the end.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 3:15"/>
    As the passage declares,
    <verse eid="HEB 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Today, should you perceive His voice,</para>
  <para style="p">do not make your hearts rigid as during the rebellion.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 3:16"/>
    For who were the ones perceiving yet rebelling? Was it not all those who departed Egypt under Moses’ guidance?
    <verse eid="HEB 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 3:17"/>
    And with whom did He experience anger across forty years? Was it not with those committing sin, whose corpses dropped in the wilderness?
    <verse eid="HEB 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 3:18"/>
    And to whom did He swear they would not enter His rest, except to those demonstrating disobedience?
    <verse eid="HEB 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 3:19"/>
    So we see they could not enter due to unbelief.
    <verse eid="HEB 3:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">7-11 Quoted from Ps. 95:7-11</para>
  <para style="p">15 Quoted from Ps. 95:7b-8</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="HEB 4"/>
  <para style="s1">The Attainment of Believers to the Sabbath Rest of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 4:1"/>
    Therefore, let us fear, lest—while the promise to enter His rest continues to stand—anyone among you should appear to have missed reaching it.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 4:2"/>
    For we too have received the gospel just as they did; yet the message they heard brought them no advantage, because they were not united by faith with those who heard it. 
    <verse eid="HEB 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 4:3"/>
    For we who have exercised faith enter that rest, just as He has stated,
    <verse eid="HEB 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Just as I swore in My anger,</para>
  <para style="p">‘They will absolutely not enter My rest,’ ”*</para>
  <para style="p">though His works reached completion from the world’s foundation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 4:4"/>
    For He has spoken somewhere regarding the seventh day in this manner: “And God rested on the seventh day from all His works.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 4:5"/>
    And once more in this passage He states, “They will absolutely not enter My rest.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 4:6"/>
    Since, therefore, it remains true that some will enter it, and those who previously received the gospel failed to enter through disobedience,
    <verse eid="HEB 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 4:7"/>
    He once more establishes a specific day—“Today”—communicating through David after considerable time, just as previously stated,
    <verse eid="HEB 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Today, should you perceive His voice,</para>
  <para style="p">do not make your hearts rigid.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 4:8"/>
    For had Joshua provided them rest, God would not have subsequently spoken about another day.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 4:9"/>
    Consequently, a Sabbath rest remains reserved for God’s people.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 4:10"/>
    For whoever has entered His rest has also ceased from his works, just as God ceased from His own.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 4:11"/>
    Let us therefore exert ourselves diligently to enter that rest, so that no one falls through following that same disobedience pattern.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 4:12"/>
    For God’s word is alive and energetically active, more penetrating than any sword sharpened on both edges, piercing to the separation point of soul and spirit, of joints and marrow, and capable of evaluating the heart’s thoughts and intentions.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 4:13"/>
    And no creature remains concealed from His sight, but everything lies exposed and laid bare before the eyes of Him to whom we must render our account.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Jesus, the Great High Priest and the Son of God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 4:14"/>
    Since, therefore, we possess a great High Priest who has traversed the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us maintain our confession firmly.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 4:15"/>
    For we do not possess a High Priest incapable of sympathising with our weaknesses, but One tested in all respects as we are, yet apart from sin.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 4:16"/>
    Let us therefore approach God’s throne of grace with boldness, so that we may receive mercy and discover grace for timely help.
    <verse eid="HEB 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">3 Quoted from Ps. 95:11</para>
  <para style="p">4 Quoted from Gen. 2:2</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Ps. 95:11</para>
  <para style="p">7 Quoted from Ps. 95:7b-8</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="HEB 5"/>
  <para style="s1">The Imperfect High Priest</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 5:1"/>
    For every high priest selected from men is appointed to act on people’s behalf in matters relating to God, to present both gifts and sacrifices addressing sins.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 5:2"/>
    He can respond gently to the ignorant and those who wander off course, since he himself experiences weakness.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 5:3"/>
    Due to this weakness, he must present sacrifices for sins, both for the people and for himself.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 5:4"/>
    And no one claims this honour independently; rather, he receives it when called by God, exactly as Aaron was.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Perfect High Priest</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 5:5"/>
    Similarly, Christ did not glorify Himself to become High Priest, but received appointment from the One who declare to Him,
    <verse eid="HEB 5:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are My Son;</para>
  <para style="p">today I have fathered You”;*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 5:6"/>
    just as He also states elsewhere,
    <verse eid="HEB 5:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are a priest forever,</para>
  <para style="p">according to the order of Melchizedek.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 5:7"/>
    Throughout His days in the flesh, He presented both prayers and supplications with intense cries and tears to the One capable of rescuing Him from death, and received a hearing due to His reverent submission.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 5:8"/>
    Though existing as the Son, He learned obedience through His suffering experiences.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 5:9"/>
    And having reached completion through those sufferings, He became the Author of eternal salvation for all who obey Him,
    <verse eid="HEB 5:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 5:10"/>
    having received God’s designation as High Priest according to the order of Melchizedek.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Spiritual Regression</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 5:11"/>
    Regarding this we have extensive explanation, yet it proves challenging to clarify, since you have become sluggish in comprehension.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 5:12"/>
    For although by now you should function as teachers, you require someone to teach you again the foundational elements of God’s revelations, and you have reached a point requiring milk instead of solid nourishment.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 5:13"/>
    For anyone who subsists on milk lacks experience in the word of righteousness, being still infantile. 
    <verse eid="HEB 5:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 5:14"/>
    But solid nourishment belongs to the mature, to those who through persistent practice have exercised their faculties to differentiate between good and evil.
    <verse eid="HEB 5:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Ps. 2:7</para>
  <para style="p">6 Quoted from Ps. 110:4</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="HEB 6"/>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Falling Away</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 6:1"/>
    Therefore, leaving behind the foundational elements of the teaching of Christ, let us advance towards maturity, not establishing again a foundation of repentance from lifeless works and faith directed towards God,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 6:2"/>
    of teaching regarding washings and hand-laying, and regarding the resurrection of the dead and eternal judgment.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 6:3"/>
    And this we will do, if God grants permission.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 6:4"/>
    For it proves impossible to restore to repentance those once enlightened, who tasted the heavenly gift, who became Holy Spirit participants,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 6:5"/>
    who tasted the good word of God and the powers of the ages to come,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 6:6"/>
    yet then fell away—impossible to renew them again to repentance, since they crucify the Son of God afresh for themselves and expose Him to public disgrace.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 6:7"/>
    For land that absorbs frequently falling rain and produces vegetation beneficial for those who cultivate it receives God's blessing.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 6:8"/>
    But land that responds by producing only thorns and weeds proves itself useless. It stands under the curse of God’s judgment, and its final outcome is destruction. 
    <verse eid="HEB 6:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 6:9"/>
    Yet, beloved ones, though speaking this way, we remain persuaded of superior things concerning you—things accompanying salvation.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 6:10"/>
    For God is not unjust to overlook your work and the love you demonstrated towards His name by serving God’s people and continuing such service.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 6:11"/>
    We desire each of you to display this same earnestness right through to the end, for the full realisation of your hope,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 6:12"/>
    so that you will not become lethargic, but will imitate those who through faith and endurance inherit the promises.  
    <verse eid="HEB 6:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Unchangeableness of God’s Promise</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 6:13"/>
    For when God made His promise to Abraham, since He could swear by none greater, He swore by Himself,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 6:14"/>
    declaring, “I will certainly bless you abundantly and multiply you greatly.”
    <verse eid="HEB 6:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 6:15"/>
    And thus, after enduring patiently, Abraham obtained what had been promised.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 6:16"/>
    For people swear by someone superior to themselves, and the oath provides confirmation ending all arguments.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 6:17"/>
    Similarly, when God desired to demonstrate more fully to the heirs of the promise the unchangeable character of His purpose, He confirmed it with an oath,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 6:18"/>
    so that through two unchangeable realities, in which God’s lying is impossible, we who have fled for refuge might possess powerful encouragement to grasp the hope lying before us.
    <verse eid="HEB 6:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 6:19"/>
    We possess this hope as our soul’s anchor, both reliable and stable, entering into the inner area behind the curtain,
    <verse eid="HEB 6:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 6:20"/>
    where Jesus entered as a forerunner for our benefit, having become a high priest forever according to the order of Melchizedek. 
    <verse eid="HEB 6:20"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="HEB 7"/>
  <para style="s1">Melchizedek, the Priest of the Most High God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 7:1"/>
    For this Melchizedek, king of Salem and priest of God Most High, encountered Abraham returning from defeating the kings and pronounced blessing on him.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 7:2"/>
    To him Abraham also apportioned a tenth of everything. His name, interpreted, signifies first king of righteousness, and then also king of Salem, signifying king of peace. 
    <verse eid="HEB 7:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 7:3"/>
    He appears without a recorded father, without a recorded mother, and without genealogy, having neither a documented beginning of days nor an end of life. In this way he resembles the Son of God and continues as a priest forever. 
    <verse eid="HEB 7:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 7:4"/>
    Now observe this man’s greatness: even patriarch Abraham gave him a tenth of the choicest plunder.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 7:5"/>
    Now those who are Levi’s descendants and receive the priestly office possess a commandment according to the Law to collect tithes from the people, meaning from their brothers, though these also descended from Abraham.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 7:6"/>
    But this one whose ancestry is not traced from them collected tithes from Abraham and blessed the one possessing the promises.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 7:7"/>
    And indisputably, the inferior receives blessing from the superior.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 7:8"/>
    In one instance, mortal men receive tithes; in the other instance, one receives them of whom it is testified that he lives.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 7:9"/>
    And, one might say, through Abraham even Levi, who receives tithes, has paid tithes,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 7:10"/>
    for he still remained in his ancestor’s body when Melchizedek encountered him.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Priesthood of Jesus According to the Order of Melchizedek</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 7:11"/>
    Now if perfection had been achievable through the Levitical priesthood, for based on it the people received the Law, what further necessity existed for another priest to arise according to the order of Melchizedek rather than being designated according to the order of Aaron?
    <verse eid="HEB 7:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 7:12"/>
    For when the priesthood undergoes change, necessarily a change of Law must also occur.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 7:13"/>
    For the One about whom these statements are made belonged to a different tribe, from which nobody has attended the altar.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 7:14"/>
    For it is obvious that our Lord descended from Judah, a tribe regarding which Moses communicated nothing concerning priests.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 7:15"/>
    This becomes even more apparent if another priest arises bearing the likeness of Melchizedek,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 7:16"/>
    who has become priest not based on a legal requirement concerning physical lineage, but based on the power of an indestructible life. 
    <verse eid="HEB 7:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 7:17"/>
    For testimony is given,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“You are a priest forever,</para>
  <para style="p">according to the order of Melchizedek.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 7:18"/>
    On one hand, a setting aside of the previous commandment occurs due to its weakness and ineffectiveness,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 7:19"/>
    for the Law brought nothing to perfection. On the other hand, an  introduction of a superior hope occurs, through which we approach God.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 7:20"/>
    And this occurred not without oath-taking. For those men became priests without an oath,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 7:21"/>
    but He with an oath through the One who said to Him,
    <verse eid="HEB 7:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“The Lord has sworn</para>
  <para style="p">and will not reverse His decision:</para>
  <para style="p">‘You are a priest forever.’ ”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 7:22"/>
    By this much greater measure, Jesus has become the guarantor of a superior covenant.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 7:23"/>
    Now the previous priests existed in greater numbers, because death prevented their continuing.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 7:24"/>
    But because He continues forever, He possesses a priesthood that does not transfer.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 7:25"/>
    Consequently, He is able to save to the uttermost and totally those who approach God through Him, since He lives forever to intercede for them.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 7:26"/>
    For such a High Priest proved fitting for us: holy, innocent, undefiled, separated from sinners, and elevated above the heavens.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 7:27"/>
    He possesses no need, as those high priests do, to present sacrifices daily, first for His own sins and subsequently for the people's, because He accomplished this once for all when He presented Himself.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 7:28"/>
    For the Law appoints men as high priests who possess weakness, but the word of the oath, coming after the Law, appoints a Son who has been perfected forever.
    <verse eid="HEB 7:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">17 Quoted from Ps. 110:4</para>
  <para style="p">21 Quoted from Ps. 110:4</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="HEB 8"/>
  <para style="s1">The Mediator of a Better Covenant and a More Excellent Ministry</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 8:1"/>
    Now the central point in what we are communicating is this: We possess such a High Priest, One who has seated Himself at the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in heaven,
    <verse eid="HEB 8:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 8:2"/>
    serving as minister in the sanctuary, meaning in the authentic tabernacle that the Lord established, not any human.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 8:3"/>
    For every high priest receives appointment to present both gifts and sacrifices; therefore it was necessary that this One also possess something to present.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 8:4"/>
    Now were He on earth, He would not qualify as priest, since priests already exist who present the gifts according to the Law.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 8:5"/>
    These serve in what constitutes a copy and shadow of heavenly realities, just as Moses received divine instruction when about to complete the tabernacle. For God stated, “Observe that you construct everything according to the pattern displayed to you on the mountain.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 8:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 8:6"/>
    But now Christ has obtained a ministry far more excellent, since He mediates a superior covenant, one enacted upon superior promises.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The New Covenant</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 8:7"/>
    For had that first covenant been faultless, no occasion would have been sought for a second.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 8:8"/>
    But finding fault with them, God states,
    <verse eid="HEB 8:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Behold, days are approaching, the Lord declares,</para>
  <para style="p">when I will bring about a new covenant</para>
  <para style="p">with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 8:9"/>
    not like the covenant I established with their ancestors
    <verse eid="HEB 8:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">on the day I grasped their hand</para>
  <para style="p">to lead them from Egypt’s land,</para>
  <para style="p">because they did not remain in My covenant,</para>
  <para style="p">and I disregarded them, the Lord declares.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 8:10"/>
    For this constitutes the covenant I will establish 
    <verse eid="HEB 8:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">with the house of Israel after those days, the Lord declares:</para>
  <para style="p">I will place My laws into their minds,</para>
  <para style="p">and inscribe them upon their hearts.</para>
  <para style="p">And I will be their God,</para>
  <para style="p">and they will be My people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 8:11"/>
    And they will no longer teach each one his neighbour,
    <verse eid="HEB 8:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and each one his brother, stating, </para>
  <para style="p">‘Know the Lord,’</para>
  <para style="p">because all will know Me,</para>
  <para style="p">from their smallest to their greatest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 8:12"/>
    For I will show mercy regarding their unrighteousness,
    <verse eid="HEB 8:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and their sins I will remember no longer.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 8:13"/>
    In calling this “new,” He has rendered the first obsolete. And what is becoming obsolete and aging is on the verge of disappearance.
    <verse eid="HEB 8:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Ex. 25:40</para>
  <para style="p">8-12 Quoted from Jer. 31:31-34</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="HEB 9"/>
  <para style="s1">The Earthly Sanctuary</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 9:1"/>
    Now the first covenant had regulations for worship and an earthly sanctuary.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 9:2"/>
    For a tent was prepared, the first section, in which were the lampstand and the table and the bread of the Presence; this is called the Holy Place.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 9:3"/>
    Behind the second curtain stood a tent called the Most Holy Place,
    <verse eid="HEB 9:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 9:4"/>
    containing the golden incense altar and the covenant ark completely overlaid with gold. Inside this were the golden jar holding the manna, Aaron’s rod that budded, and the covenant tablets.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 9:5"/>
    Above it stood the cherubim of glory overshadowing the mercy seat. But we cannot now discuss these items in detail.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 9:6"/>
    With these arrangements thus prepared, the priests enter the first tent constantly, conducting their ministry.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 9:7"/>
    But into the second tent only the high priest enters, once annually, never without blood, which he presents for himself and for the sins of the people committed in ignorance.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 9:8"/>
    The Holy Spirit indicates through this that the way into the holy places has not yet been revealed while the first tent still stands.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 9:9"/>
    This serves as an illustration for the present time, showing that the gifts and sacrifices being presented cannot perfect the conscience of the worshipper.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 9:10"/>
    These consist only of food and drink and various washings, regulations for the body imposed until the time of reformation.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Eternal Redemption</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 9:11"/>
    But Christ appeared as High Priest of the good things that have come, passing through the greater and more complete tent not made with hands, meaning not of this creation.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 9:12"/>
    He entered once for all into the holy places, not through the blood of goats and calves but through His own blood, having secured eternal redemption.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 9:13"/>
    For if the blood of goats and bulls, and the ashes of a heifer sprinkled on the defiled, sanctify for bodily purification,
    <verse eid="HEB 9:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 9:14"/>
    how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit presented Himself unblemished to God, cleanse our conscience from dead works to serve the living God.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 9:15"/>
    For this very reason, Christ serves as the mediator of a new covenant: through His sacrificial death, which secures release from the transgressions committed under the former covenant, those whom God has called may now receive the promised eternal inheritance. 
    <verse eid="HEB 9:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 9:16"/>
    For where a testament exists, the death of the testator must be established.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 9:17"/>
    For a testament takes effect only at death, since it has no force while the testator lives.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 9:18"/>
    Consequently, not even the first covenant was inaugurated without blood.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 9:19"/>
    For when Moses had proclaimed every commandment according to the Law to all the people, he took the blood of calves and goats with water and scarlet wool and hyssop, and sprinkled both the scroll itself and all the people,
    <verse eid="HEB 9:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 9:20"/>
    stating, “This is the blood of the covenant that God commanded for you.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 9:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 9:21"/>
    And similarly he sprinkled both the tent and all the ministry vessels with blood.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 9:22"/>
    Indeed according to the Law, almost everything receives purification with blood, and without the shedding of blood forgiveness does not occur.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 9:23"/>
    Therefore it was necessary for the copies of the heavenly things to be purified with these sacrifices, but the heavenly things themselves with superior sacrifices to these.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 9:24"/>
    For Christ did not enter holy places made with hands, copies of the authentic ones, but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God on our behalf.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 9:25"/>
    Nor did He enter to present Himself repeatedly, as the high priest enters the holy places annually with blood not his own.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 9:26"/>
    Otherwise He would have needed to suffer repeatedly since the foundation of the world. But now, once at the consummation of the ages, He has been revealed to remove sin through His sacrifice.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 9:27"/>
    And just as it is appointed for people to die once, and after this judgment,
    <verse eid="HEB 9:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 9:28"/>
    so Christ, having been presented once to bear the sins of many people, will appear a second time, apart from sin, to those eagerly awaiting Him for salvation.
    <verse eid="HEB 9:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">20 Quoted from Ex. 24:8</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="HEB 10"/>
  <para style="s1">Christ’s Once-for-all Sacrifice</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 10:1"/>
    For the Law has a shadow of the coming good things, not the actual form of the realities. It can never, through the same sacrifices offered continually year after year, perfect those who approach.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 10:2"/>
    Otherwise, would they not have ceased being presented, because the worshippers, once cleansed, would no longer have consciousness of sins?
    <verse eid="HEB 10:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 10:3"/>
    But in these sacrifices there is an annual reminder of sins.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 10:4"/>
    For the blood of bulls and goats cannot remove sins.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 10:5"/>
    Therefore, entering the world, He states,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Sacrifice and offering You did not desire,</para>
  <para style="p">but a body You prepared for Me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 10:6"/>
    In burnt offerings and sin offerings
    <verse eid="HEB 10:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">You took no pleasure.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 10:7"/>
    Then I said, ‘Behold, I have come—
    <verse eid="HEB 10:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">in the scroll of the book it is written about Me—</para>
  <para style="p">to do Your will, O God.’ ”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 10:8"/>
    After saying above, “Sacrifices and offerings and burnt offerings and sin offerings You did not desire, nor did You take pleasure in them”*—which are presented according to the Law—
    <verse eid="HEB 10:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 10:9"/>
    then He stated, “Behold, I have come to do Your will.”* He removes the first to establish the second.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 10:10"/>
    By that will we have been sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 10:11"/>
    And every priest stands daily ministering and offering repeatedly the same sacrifices, which can never remove sins.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 10:12"/>
    But this One, having offered one sacrifice for sins for all time, sat down at the right hand of God, 
    <verse eid="HEB 10:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 10:13"/>
    thereafter waiting until His enemies are placed as a footstool for His feet.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 10:14"/>
    For by one offering He has perfected for all time those who are being sanctified.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 10:15"/>
    And the Holy Spirit also testifies to us, for after stating,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 10:16"/>
    “This is the covenant I will establish with them
    <verse eid="HEB 10:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">after those days, the Lord declares:</para>
  <para style="p">I will put My laws upon their hearts,</para>
  <para style="p">and upon their minds I will inscribe them,”</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 10:17"/>
    then He adds,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“Their sins and their lawless deeds</para>
  <para style="p">I will remember no more.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 10:18"/>
    Now where forgiveness of these exists, there is no longer an offering for sin.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Drawing Near to God’s Presence</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 10:19"/>
    Therefore, brothers and sisters, since we have confidence to enter the holy places through the blood of Jesus,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 10:20"/>
    by a new and living way He inaugurated for us through the curtain, meaning His flesh,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 10:21"/>
    and since we have a great priest over the household of God,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 10:22"/>
    let us approach with a sincere heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled clean from a wicked conscience and our bodies washed with pure water.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 10:23"/>
    Let us maintain the confession of our hope unwavering, for the One who promised is faithful.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 10:24"/>
    And let us consider how to provoke one another to love and good works,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 10:25"/>
    not abandoning our assembling together, as some practise habitually, but encouraging one another, and all the more as you see the Day approaching.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Deliberate Sinning</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 10:26"/>
    For if we sin deliberately after receiving the knowledge of the truth, no sacrifice for sins remains any longer.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 10:27"/>
    Rather, a terrifying expectation of judgment and a fury of fire about to consume the adversaries.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 10:28"/>
    Anyone who rejects the Law of Moses will be put to death based on the testimony of two or three witnesses, with no showing of mercy.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 10:29"/>
    How much worse punishment do you think will be deserved by the one who has trampled the Son of God underfoot, and has regarded as common the covenant blood by which he was sanctified, and has insulted the Spirit of grace?
    <verse eid="HEB 10:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="HEB 10:30"/>
    For we know the One who stated, “Vengeance belongs to Me; I will repay.”* And again, “The Lord will judge His people.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 10:30"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="HEB 10:31"/>
    It is terrifying to fall into the hands of the living God. 
    <verse eid="HEB 10:31"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Reward of Faith and Endurance</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="HEB 10:32"/>
    But remember the earlier days when, after being enlightened, you endured a great suffering struggle.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:32"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="HEB 10:33"/>
    Sometimes being publicly exposed to insults and afflictions, and sometimes becoming partners with those experiencing this treatment.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:33"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="HEB 10:34"/>
    For you sympathised with the prisoners and joyfully accepted the seizure of your possessions, knowing you possess a superior and enduring possession.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:34"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="HEB 10:35"/>
    Therefore, do not discard your confidence, which carries great reward.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:35"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="HEB 10:36"/>
    For you have need of endurance, so that after doing the will of God, you may receive what is promised.
    <verse eid="HEB 10:36"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="HEB 10:37"/>
    “For yet a very little while,
    <verse eid="HEB 10:37"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">the Coming One will come and will not delay.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="HEB 10:38"/>
    But My righteous one will live by faith;
    <verse eid="HEB 10:38"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and if he shrinks back,</para>
  <para style="p">My soul has no pleasure in him.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="HEB 10:39"/>
    But we are not among those who shrink back to destruction, but among those who have faith resulting in the preservation of the soul.   
    <verse eid="HEB 10:39"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5-7 Quoted from Ps. 40:6-8</para>
  <para style="p">8 Quoted from Ps. 40:6</para>
  <para style="p">9 Quoted from Ps. 40:8</para>
  <para style="p">16-17 Quoted from Jer. 31:33-34</para>
  <para style="p">30 Quoted from Deut. 32:35</para>
  <para style="p">30 Quoted from Deut. 32:36</para>
  <para style="p">37-38 Quoted from Hab. 2:3-4</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="HEB 11"/>
  <para style="s1">The Witnesses of Faith</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 11:1"/>
    Now faith is the settled confidence in what God has promised but not yet seen, and the firm inner certainty concerning realities that remain invisible.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 11:2"/>
    For by this faith the people of ancient times received the approval of God. 
    <verse eid="HEB 11:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 11:3"/>
    By faith we come to understand that the universe was prepared by the spoken word of God, so that what is visible did not originate from material things that could be seen.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 11:4"/>
    By faith Abel presented to God a sacrifice that was superior to Cain’s, and through it he was attested to be righteous, with God Himself testifying to the worth of his offering. Through this act of faith, though he has died, he continues to speak.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 11:5"/>
    By faith Enoch was taken from this life so that he did not experience death, and he could not be found because God removed him. Prior to being taken, he had received the testimony that his life pleased God.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 11:6"/>
    And apart from faith it is impossible to please God, because the one who comes near to Him must believe that He truly exists and that He rewards those who diligently seek Him.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 11:7"/>
    By faith Noah, having been warned by God about events that had not yet occurred, responded with reverent obedience and constructed an ark to save his household. By this faith he exposed the unbelief of the world and became an heir of the righteousness that comes by faith.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 11:8"/>
    By faith Abraham obeyed when he was called to leave and go to a place that he would later receive as an inheritance. He went out in obedience, even though he did not know where he was going.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 11:9"/>
    By faith he lived as a resident alien in the land of promise, dwelling in tents along with Isaac and Jacob, who shared in the same promise.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 11:10"/>
    For he was looking ahead to the city with permanent foundations, whose architect and builder is God.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 11:11"/>
    By faith Sarah herself was enabled to conceive, even beyond the normal age for childbearing, because she regarded the One who had promised as faithful.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 11:12"/>
    Therefore, even from one man who was as good as dead, God brought forth a countless number of descendants—so many they can be compared to the stars in the sky or the grains of sand along the seashore.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 11:13"/>
    All of these died while trusting God, without receiving the promised fulfilment, but they saw it from a distance, welcomed it, and openly confessed that they were strangers and temporary residents on the earth.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 11:14"/>
    Those who speak in this way clearly show that they are seeking a homeland of their own.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 11:15"/>
    If they had continued to think about the land they left behind, they would have had the opportunity to return.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 11:16"/>
    Instead, they longed for a better country, that is, a heavenly one. For this reason, God is not ashamed to be called their God, because He has prepared a city for them.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 11:17"/>
    By faith Abraham, when God tested him, offered up Isaac. The one who had received the promises was in the act of offering his only son,
    <verse eid="HEB 11:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 11:18"/>
    concerning whom it had been said, “Through Isaac your offspring will be named.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 11:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 11:19"/>
    He reasoned that God was able even to raise the dead, and in a figurative sense, he did receive Isaac back from death.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 11:20"/>
    By faith Isaac spoke blessings over Jacob and Esau concerning future events.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 11:21"/>
    By faith Jacob, as he was dying, blessed each of Joseph’s sons and worshipped God while leaning upon the top of his staff.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 11:22"/>
    By faith Joseph, near the end of his life, spoke about the future departure of the sons of Israel and gave instructions concerning his bones.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 11:23"/>
    By faith Moses was hidden for three months by his parents after his birth, because they saw that the child was special, and they did not fear the king’s command.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 11:24"/>
    By faith Moses, when he had grown to maturity, refused to be identified as the son of Pharaoh’s daughter.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 11:25"/>
    He chose instead to share in suffering with the people of God rather than to enjoy the temporary pleasures of sin.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 11:26"/>
    He regarded the disgrace associated with Christ as greater wealth than the treasures of Egypt, because he was fixing his attention on the reward that was yet to come.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 11:27"/>
    By faith he left Egypt, not fearing the anger of the king, for he endured as though seeing the One who is invisible.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 11:28"/>
    By faith he observed the Passover and the sprinkling of the blood, so that the destroyer of the firstborn would not strike them.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 11:29"/>
    By faith the people crossed the Red Sea as if on dry ground, but when the Egyptians attempted the same, they were engulfed.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="HEB 11:30"/>
    By faith the walls of Jericho collapsed after they had been encircled for seven days.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:30"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="HEB 11:31"/>
    By faith Rahab the prostitute was spared from destruction along with those who disobeyed, because she welcomed the spies in peace.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:31"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="HEB 11:32"/>
    And what more should I say? Time would fail me to recount the accounts of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets,
    <verse eid="HEB 11:32"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="HEB 11:33"/>
    who through faith conquered kingdoms, carried out justice, obtained what God had promised, shut the mouths of lions,
    <verse eid="HEB 11:33"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="HEB 11:34"/>
    extinguished the force of fire, escaped the blade of the sword, gained strength from weakness, became powerful in battle, and routed foreign armies.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:34"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="HEB 11:35"/>
    Women received their dead raised back to life. Others were tortured to death, refusing release, so that they might attain a better resurrection.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:35"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="HEB 11:36"/>
    Still others endured mocking and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:36"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="HEB 11:37"/>
    They were stoned, they were sawn in two, they were put to death by the sword. They wandered about clothed in sheepskins and goatskins, lacking necessities, afflicted, and mistreated—
    <verse eid="HEB 11:37"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="HEB 11:38"/>
    people of whom the world was not worthy—roaming in deserts and mountains and living in caves and holes in the ground.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:38"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="HEB 11:39"/>
    And all of these, though they received the approval of God because of their faith, did not obtain the promised fulfilment,
    <verse eid="HEB 11:39"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="HEB 11:40"/>
    because God had planned something better for us, so that apart from us they would not be made perfect or experience the complete fulfilment of His promises.
    <verse eid="HEB 11:40"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">18 Quoted from Gen. 21:12</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="HEB 12"/>
  <para style="s1">Jesus, the Pioneer and Completer of Faith</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 12:1"/>
    Therefore, since we are encircled by such a great multitude of witnesses who testify to a life of faith, let us strip away every hindrance and the sin that clings so tightly, and let us run with perseverance the course laid out before us.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 12:2"/>
    Let us direct our full attention to Jesus, the Originator and Perfecter of our faith. For the joy that lay ahead of Him, He endured the cross, giving no regard to its disgrace, and He has taken His place at the right hand of the throne of God.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Exhortation Concerning the Lord’s Discipline</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 12:3"/>
    Reflect carefully on the One who endured such intense hostility from sinners directed against Himself, so that you do not grow exhausted or collapse inwardly.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 12:4"/>
    In your struggle against sin, you have not yet been pressed to the point of shedding your blood.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 12:5"/>
    Yet you have neglected the encouragement that addresses you as sons:
    <verse eid="HEB 12:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“My son, do not treat the discipline of the Lord as insignificant,</para>
  <para style="p">and do not lose courage when He corrects you;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 12:6"/>
    for the Lord disciplines the one He loves,
    <verse eid="HEB 12:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">and He flogs every son whom He accepts.”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 12:7"/>
    Endure hardship as divine discipline; God is dealing with you as sons. What son is there whom a father does not discipline?
    <verse eid="HEB 12:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 12:8"/>
    But if you are left without such discipline—something all true sons experience—then you are illegitimate and not genuine children.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 12:9"/>
    Furthermore, we respected our earthly fathers when they corrected us. Should we not all the more subject ourselves to the Father of spirits and truly live?
    <verse eid="HEB 12:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 12:10"/>
    They disciplined us for a short time according to their limited judgment, but God disciplines us for our good, so that we may participate in His holiness.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 12:11"/>
    All discipline is painful at the time rather than pleasant, yet afterwards it yields a harvest of peace and righteousness for those shaped by it.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 12:12"/>
    Therefore, strengthen drooping hands and steady weakened knees.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 12:13"/>
    Mark out straight paths for your feet, so that what is impaired will not be put out of joint, but instead be restored.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Call to Peace and Holiness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 12:14"/>
    Actively pursue peace with everyone, and pursue holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 12:15"/>
    Watch carefully that no one falls short of the grace of God, that no bitter root grows up to cause trouble and corrupt many.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 12:16"/>
    Ensure that no one among you is sexually immoral or godless like Esau, who traded his birthright for a single meal.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 12:17"/>
    For you know that later, when he desired to receive the blessing, he was rejected; he found no opportunity to undo his choice, even though he sought it with tears.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Greater Reality to Which We Have Come</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 12:18"/>
    You have not approached something tangible—a blazing mountain surrounded by darkness, gloom, and storm,
    <verse eid="HEB 12:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 12:19"/>
    nor the blast of a trumpet or a voice whose words caused those who heard it to beg that nothing further be spoken to them.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 12:20"/>
    For the people could not endure the strict command given to them: “If even an animal touches the mountain, it must be stoned.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 12:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="HEB 12:21"/>
    The sight was so terrifying that Moses said, “I am filled with fear and trembling.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 12:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 12:22"/>
    But you have come to Mount Zion—to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem—to countless angels gathered in joyful assembly,
    <verse eid="HEB 12:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 12:23"/>
    to the congregation of the firstborn whose names are recorded in heaven, to God the Judge of all, to the spirits of righteous people brought to perfection,
    <verse eid="HEB 12:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 12:24"/>
    and to Jesus, the mediator of a new covenant, and to blood that has been sprinkled, speaking a message superior to the blood of Abel.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Rejecting God’s Voice</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 12:25"/>
    Be certain that you do not refuse the One who is speaking. For if those who rejected the earthly warning did not escape, how much less will we escape if we turn away from the One who speaks from heaven?
    <verse eid="HEB 12:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="HEB 12:26"/>
    At that time His voice shook the earth, but now He has promised: “Once more I will shake not only the earth, but also the heavens.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 12:26"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="HEB 12:27"/>
    This phrase “once more” indicates the removal of what can be shaken—that is, created things—so that what cannot be shaken may remain.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:27"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="HEB 12:28"/>
    Therefore, since we are receiving a kingdom that cannot be shaken, let us respond with gratitude, and by it offer worship that is pleasing to God, marked by reverence and deep awe,
    <verse eid="HEB 12:28"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="HEB 12:29"/>
    for our God is indeed a consuming fire.
    <verse eid="HEB 12:29"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5-6 Quoted from Prov. 3:11-12</para>
  <para style="p">20 Quoted from Ex. 19:12-13</para>
  <para style="p">21 Quoted from Deut. 9:19</para>
  <para style="p">26 Quoted from Haggai 2:6</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="HEB 13"/>
  <para style="s1">Concluding Exhortations</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HEB 13:1"/>
    Continue to love one another sincerely, as members of the same family of faith.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HEB 13:2"/>
    Do not neglect showing hospitality; in doing so, some have unknowingly welcomed angels into their homes.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HEB 13:3"/>
    Remember those who are imprisoned as if you were in chains with them, and those who are mistreated as if you were experiencing it yourself.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="HEB 13:4"/>
    Honour marriage, and keep the marriage bed pure, for God will judge those who are sexually immoral and adulterers.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HEB 13:5"/>
    Keep your life free from greed, and be satisfied with what you have, for God has promised, “I will never leave you, nor will I ever forsake you.”*
    <verse eid="HEB 13:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HEB 13:6"/>
    Therefore, we can confidently declare: 
    <verse eid="HEB 13:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">“The Lord is my helper; I will not fear. </para>
  <para style="p">What can anyone do to me?”*</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HEB 13:7"/>
    Remember your leaders, who spoke to you God’s word. Reflect on how their lives turned out, and follow the example of their faith.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="HEB 13:8"/>
    Jesus Christ remains unchanging—yesterday, today, and forever.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="HEB 13:9"/>
    Do not be swayed by diverse and strange or novel teachings. It is better for the heart to be strengthened by God’s grace than by rituals or foods, which have not benefited those who focus on them.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HEB 13:10"/>
    We have a spiritual altar, from which those serving in the old tabernacle could not partake.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="HEB 13:11"/>
    The blood of animals brought into the sanctuary as sin offerings was burned outside the camp.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HEB 13:12"/>
    In the same way, Jesus suffered outside the city gate, to make the people holy through His own blood.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HEB 13:13"/>
    Let us, then, go to Him outside the camp, bearing the shame He bore.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HEB 13:14"/>
    We do not have a permanent city here, but we are seeking the one to come.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HEB 13:15"/>
    Therefore, through Jesus, let us continually offer to God a sacrifice of praise, the fruit of lips that acknowledge His name.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="HEB 13:16"/>
    Do not neglect doing good and sharing with others; such sacrifices please God.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="HEB 13:17"/>
    Obey and submit to your leaders, for they watch over your souls. Let them do this willingly, not reluctantly, for that would be harmful to you.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Request for Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="HEB 13:18"/>
    Pray for us, for we are confident that we live with a good conscience, desiring to act honourably in all things.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="HEB 13:19"/>
    I urge you all the more to pray, so that I may be restored to you more quickly.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Prayer and Doxology</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HEB 13:20"/>
    Now may the God of peace, who raised from the dead the great Shepherd of the sheep, our Lord Jesus, equip you with everything good to accomplish His will, working in us what is pleasing in His sight, through Jesus Christ, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="HEB 13:22"/>
    I urge you, brothers, to accept this word of exhortation; indeed, I have written to you briefly.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HEB 13:23"/>
    Know that our brother Timothy has been released. If he comes soon, I will see you with him.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="HEB 13:24"/>
    Greet all your leaders and all the saints. Those from Italy send their greetings.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="HEB 13:25"/>
    May grace be with all of you.
    <verse eid="HEB 13:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">5 Quoted from Jos. 1:5</para>
  <para style="p">6 Quoted from Ps. 118:6</para>
  <chapter eid="HEB 13"/>
</usx>
